source	R. Descartes, Discourse on Method (1637), part IV, tr. J. Veitch
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 59, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/59
class	inference
at	S1	In the next place, I attentively examined what I was
fault	from what can and cannot be supposed (doubted) of the self and the body to their being distinct: what one can doubt of a thing is not a property of it
reference	A. Arnauld, Fourth Objections; standard as the "masked man" fallacy
